{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstdint>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing int64 = int64_t;\nconst int64 INFINITY = 1000000000000000000LL;\n\nvector<int> memoization;\n\nint recursive_solve(int64 n) {\n    if (n == 0) return 0;\n    if (n < (int64)memoization.size() && memoization[n]) return memoization[n];\n    \n    int64 num = 1;\n    int steps = 0;\n    int64 prev_delta = INFINITY;\n    \n    while (llabs(num - n) <= prev_delta) {\n        prev_delta = llabs(num - n);\n        num = num * 10 + 1;\n        steps++;\n    }\n    \n    num /= 10;\n    \n    if (num > n && num / 10 > 0) {\n        int path1 = steps + recursive_solve(llabs(num - n));\n        int path2 = (steps - 1) + recursive_solve(llabs(num / 10 - n));\n        int best = min(path1, path2);\n        if (n < (int64)memoization.size()) memoization[n] = best;\n        return best;\n    } else {\n        int final = steps + recursive_solve(llabs(num - n));\n        if (n < (int64)memoization.size()) memoization[n] = final;\n        return final;\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n#ifdef NEKROLM\n    freopen(\"input.txt\", \"r\", stdin);\n    freopen(\"output.txt\", \"w\", stdout);\n#endif\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int64 n_val;\n    cin >> n_val;\n    \n    memoization.resize(10000000, 0);\n    cout << recursive_solve(n_val);\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nsys.setrecursionlimit(1000000)\n\nINFINITY = 1000000000000000000\n\nmemoization = []\n\ndef recursive_solve(n):\n    global memoization\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n < len(memoization) and memoization[n] != 0:\n        return memoization[n]\n    \n    num = 1\n    steps = 0\n    prev_delta = INFINITY\n    \n    while abs(num - n) <= prev_delta:\n        prev_delta = abs(num - n)\n        num = num * 10 + 1\n        steps += 1\n    \n    num //= 10\n    \n    if num > n and num // 10 > 0:\n        path1 = steps + recursive_solve(abs(num - n))\n        path2 = (steps - 1) + recursive_solve(abs(num // 10 - n))\n        best = min(path1, path2)\n        if n < len(memoization):\n            memoization[n] = best\n        return best\n    else:\n        final = steps + recursive_solve(abs(num - n))\n        if n < len(memoization):\n            memoization[n] = final\n        return final\n\ndef main():\n    global memoization\n    n_val = int(input().strip())\n    \n    memoization = [0] * 10000000\n    print(recursive_solve(n_val))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.679325739853084e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.006800720002502203, -0.0007656264933757484, -0.06197052821516991, -0.6874307990074158, -9.536738616588991e-07, -9.417090768693015e-05, -3.528532761265524e-05, -2.2411095415009186e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.1012910008430481, -0.